    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Is this study a survey, observational study, or experimental study? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Does this mean that watching television for at least 2 hours every night lowers energy in the evening? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If you were to do your own experiment to determine if watching television for at least 2 hours every night lowers energy in the evening, how would you set up the experiment?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes it is not feasible or ethical for a researcher to directly influence factors as required for an experimental study. In those situations, a researcher may try to find what is called a natural experiment. While technically a form…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, in Oregon in the early 2000s, the state did not not have enough money to fund a health insurance program for everyone who would have been eligible for it, so after people applied, they randomly selected who would be allowed to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What are some statistical questions that researchers may be interested in studying, that could be answered with an experimental study, but for which a natural experiment may be necessary? Explain why an experimental study wouldn’t be…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Three of the best ways to collect data are through surveys, experimental studies, and observational studies. Each method has advantages and disadvantages depending on the question you are trying to answer.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A statistical study begins with a research question, which describes what you want to know clearly and simply. Most research questions are questions about characteristics of a population or about the effect of one variable on another.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes researchers have a question about a population, like: “What percentage of the fish in Lake Erie are toxic for humans to eat?” Sometimes they have a question about how two or more populations compare, like: “Which lake, Lake Erie…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "There are three methods for collecting data: observational studies, surveys, and experimental studies. In an experimental study, the researcher deliberately does something to one or more groups of individuals, such as giving them access to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In an observational study, the researcher records values for one or more variables, like ZIP code or height, for each individual participating in the study. These values can be obtained by observation, measurements, or taken from existing…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A researcher can also collect data with a survey, in which they ask each participant to answer one or more questions.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Each method comes with advantages and limitations that the researcher must understand before planning a study. The method used to collect data also affects what kind of conclusions can be drawn. Choosing the best method for a research…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-029",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "An experimental study collects data by directly influencing something to determine how another thing is changed.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-030",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "An observational study collects data without influencing the subjects directly.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-031",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "observational study",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L02-ACTIVITY-032",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Relaxing Television",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A survey is a set of questions given to people to seek their responses.",
